# Changes that need no evidence. A PR whose changed files all match a line here (or are tests in
# test-paths, or are in .shipinetics/) opens with no evidence, and CI passes it with no label.
# Any other file needs evidence: a recording or a terminal transcript (shipinetics:evidence).
# One bash glob per line, relative to the repo root. * matches across folders. A # starts a comment.
# This file replaces the built-in defaults, so keep the lines you still want.
# Check a path with: shipinetics-config match no-evidence-paths <path>
#
# Add a line only for files that can't change what a user sees or what the app does.
# Examples to consider: *.lock, package-lock.json (a dependency bump still runs the verify),
# infra/*, scripts/dev/*.

docs/*
*.md
.github/*
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
.vscode/*
LICENSE*
